      "source": [
        "# ITAI 1378 — Module 07 Lab\n",
        "# Controlled Generation Study\n",
        "\n",
        "**Course:** ITAI 1378 — Artificial Intelligence & Computer Vision\n",
        "**Lab:** Module 07 — Controlled Generation\n",
        "\n",
        "In this lab you use a pretrained generative model **as a tool**. You will:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Run a text-to-image pipeline (Diffusers / Stable Diffusion).\n",
        "2. Lock a seed so your results are reproducible.\n",
        "3. Change **one setting at a time** — guidance, steps, seed — and observe the effect.\n",
        "4. Use a negative prompt.\n",
        "5. Edit one of **your own** photos with img2img or inpainting.\n",
        "6. Deliberately trigger a known failure mode and explain it in plain English.\n",
        "\n",
        "The point is **judgment, not pretty pictures.**\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### Read before you start\n",
        "- Write the `# TODO` code yourself. You may use the [Diffusers documentation](https://huggingface.co/docs/diffusers). **Do not** use a text AI to write your code, captions, or reflection.\n",
        "- Keep **one fixed prompt** for all of Part A. Change only the one setting each part asks for.\n",
        "- Every Part A image must use your **signature seed** (the last five digits of your student ID) unless a part tells you to change it.\n",
        "- Caption every image with `seed / steps / guidance`. The `save_image()` helper does this for you automatically — use it.\n",
        "- Part A images must be reproducible. The instructor may re-run your stated settings.\n",
        "- Part B must use a photo **you took yourself**. Stock or AI-generated inputs are not accepted."
      ]
    },
